      <MissionDesc>Our vision is to see every youth leader thrive in deeper connection with God and each other so that every young person is changed by the story of Jesus. We create collaborative spaces for youth leaders to be personally encouraged, professionallyequipped and spiritually strengthened for faithful and effective ministry with the next generation.</MissionDesc>
      <SignificantNewProgramSrvcInd>false</SignificantNewProgramSrvcInd>
      <SignificantChangeInd>false</SignificantChangeInd>
      <ExpenseAmt>984467</ExpenseAmt>
      <Desc>Empowering Youth Leaders for Sustainable MinistryNNYM responded to the growing crisis of ministry burnout by expanding support systems for youth leaders nationwide. In 2024, we strengthened 583 local networks across more than 1,800 communities, launched our "We See You" campaign during Pastor Appreciation Month to affirm leaders, and actively trained network coordinators to foster connection, prayer, and peer support. These collaborative spaces help combat isolation, elevate care, and encourage longevity in ministry. Our goal remains clear: to ensure that every youth leader is spiritually supported, relationally connected, and equipped to thrive.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>302913</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>Raising Up the Next Generation of Ministry LeadersAmid rising leadership vacancies and shifting youth culture, NNYM joined forces with partners like GLS Next Gen, NXT Move North America, and Dare 2 Share to invest in the future of the Church. We supported youth leaders in training and empowering students for evangelism and leadership. Fueled by movements like the Asbury revival and national camp commitments, thousands of teenagers responded to vocational ministry in 2024. Together, we are igniting a generational shift where young people are stepping into leadership todaynot just preparing for it tomorrow.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>227184</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>Mobilizing a Nationwide Prayer MovementIn 2024, NNYM launched the Prayer Symphony initiative, a unified effort to mobilize churches, ministries, and individuals to pray for every school and juvenile detention center in America. Through strategic partnerships with over a dozen ministries, we helped coordinate prayer at 1,627 campuses during one week in August alone and saw over 900 schools newly adopted for ongoing prayer. With more than 35,000 prayer champions and a presence on 52,000+ campuses, this movement is harmonizing prayer efforts for a generation in need of spiritual covering.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
